14. VISUAL VERIFICATION & ITERATIVE IMPROVEMENT
========================================================

This requirement is mandatory.

A successful build does NOT mean the graphics are good.

Use an iterative visual inspection process.

When browser automation and screenshot capture are available:

1. Start the application.
2. Capture a desktop screenshot.
3. Capture mobile portrait and landscape screenshots.
4. Capture the initial scene.
5. Capture the scene during an animated event.
6. Capture the scene after a meaningful interaction.
7. Inspect the actual rendered output.
8. Identify deficiencies in composition, geometry, lighting, texture quality, animation, framing, and UI.
9. Correct the deficiencies.
10. Repeat for at least three meaningful visual-improvement iterations where feasible.

Use Playwright or an equivalent browser inspection tool when available.

For repeatable visual tests, stabilize nondeterministic animation, timing, randomness, and browser conditions.

When tools cannot inspect screenshots directly, generate the available artifacts, execute the available tests, and clearly identify what remains unverified.

Never claim visual validation was performed when no image was actually inspected.

SCORING RUBRIC (1 TO 5):
- Art direction and visual cohesion
- Geometry and material quality
- Lighting and depth
- Environmental richness
- Animation and liveliness
- Interaction quality
- Camera behavior
- Mobile appearance
- Performance and fluidity

Aim for at least 4/5 in each area under genuine inspection.

Scores are evaluation aids, not evidence by themselves.

Do not fabricate measurements or assessments to meet the score.

